// Recording a room.
//
// A recording is a hosted recorder attached to a room as a recording watchdog:
// a subscriber with no publish rights that receives what any viewer would and
// writes it to storage. It is disclosed to the room the way every watchdog is,
// and it is billed the way every viewer is -- for the bytes it receives -- plus
// storage at cost. There is no recording fee.
//
// What is written depends on the room's encryption policy, and the API says
// which rather than leaving a customer to discover it from the files:
//
// - Always, a lossless archive of every object as it arrived, with its group,
//   object ID and timing. In a room that requires end-to-end encryption this
//   is ciphertext, and only the customer's keys open it.
// - Additionally, in a room whose media travels in the clear, a CMAF (fMP4)
//   rendition per track where the codec can be remuxed without transcoding.

